## Glyphs

`beta1/src/fbvdu.bas` carries bitmap glyph data as `DATA` statements. Most of
it is generated from geometry and owes nobody anything; two families do not.

**DejaVu Sans Mono** — under the **Bitstream Vera Fonts Copyright**
(Bitstream, Inc.) with Public Domain additions by the DejaVu authors.
Rasterised to 8x8 by `beta1/tools/mklatin.py`, `mksym.py` and `mkdbox.py` for
part of the Latin-1 block, a couple of dozen symbols, and the double
box-drawing set. The licence permits modification and redistribution; note its
naming clause — do not call a derived font "DejaVu".

**Nerd Fonts** — 27 icons in slots 276-302, rasterised by
`beta1/tools/mkicons.py` from a Nerd Font build. Nerd Fonts aggregates several
upstreams under different terms, and these 27 draw on:

| Source | Licence |
|---|---|
| Font Awesome (free) | **CC-BY-4.0** — attribution required, which is this row |
| Material Design Icons | Apache-2.0 |
| Octicons | MIT |
| Devicons | MIT |
| Powerline | MIT |
| Seti-UI | MIT |

**Generated, and owing nothing:** braille (U+2800-28FF), the block elements
(U+2580-259F), sextants and octants, and the legacy diagonals (U+1FB3C-1FB8B)
are all computed — the last of those from Unicode's own character *names*,
because no font on the build machine contained them. See `beta1/docs/glyphs.md`.

**Not included:** the 8x8 font the engine harvests off the Raspberry Pi's VDU
driver at run time. Those glyphs belong to that driver, so no copy is
distributed here. `beta1/test/fbfont.bas` harvests it from your own machine.

